          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.846,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "Write the following fractions as a sum of fractions and also as decimals:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.124,
            0.844,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "| Fraction | Expanding the Numerator | Sum of one-tenths, one-hundredths, one-thousands,... | Decimals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 2541000 | 1200000 +10 5000 +10 400=1 20 +10 50 +10 400 | 0.2 + 0.05 + 0.004 | 0.254 |\n| 84710000 |  |  |  |\n| 173100 |  |  |  |\n| 231000 |  |  |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.574,
            0.815,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": "? Can you give a simple rule to divide any number by a number of the form 1 followed by zeroes — 10, 100, 1000, etc.? For example, ${ \\frac { 1 2 3 } { 1 0 } } ,$ $\\frac { 2 4 } { 1 0 0 }   \\mathrm { o r }   \\frac { 6 7 8 } { 1 0 0 0 }   ?$ Look for a pattern in the previous problems."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.671,
            0.73,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": "Here is one such rule. Let us consider the example $1 2 3 \\div 1 0 .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.695,
            0.837,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "**Step 1:** Write the dividend as it is and place a decimal point at the end. 123."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.744,
            0.636,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "**Step 2:** Count the number of zeroes in the divisor."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.768,
            0.356,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": "10 \\to 1    zero",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.792,
            0.848,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": "**Step 3:** Move the decimal point from Step 1 left by the same number of places as the count from Step 2. Add zeroes in front if needed."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.934,
            0.187,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": "68"
        }
      ]
    }
